text = "[center][color=gold]The Chronicles of the Sun-Kings[/color][/center]

For thousands of years, the history of the African continent was protected by the Sun-Kings. They held their power not in swords, but in the [color=gold]Sun-Scrolls[/color] — a collection of every innovation, proverb, and trade secret from the North to the South.

This knowledge was kept in a magical golden jar, guarded by the Great Shaman, [color=cyan]Muzu[/color].

[color=red]However, a shadow known as \"The Eclipse\" grew jealous of this light.[/color] It shattered the golden jar, scattering the history of the continent to the winds. People forgot how to trade fairly, how to build great stone walls, and how to read the stars. The world began to lose its color.

[color=lime]You are a young apprentice Griot[/color] — the only one who can still see the faint glimmer of lost history. Muzu, now a spirit guide, calls out to you. He gives you the [color=gold]Griot's Compass[/color], which points toward lost knowledge.

[center][color=yellow]═══════════════════════════════[/color][/center]

[center][b]Your Quest: Restore the Sun-Scrolls[/b][/center]

[color=gold] The Golden Courts of Wagadugu[/color]
Reach Level 10 to learn the value of fair exchange and trade.

[color=cyan] The Libraries of the North[/color]
Reach Level 20 to rediscover the math and architecture that built the pyramids.

[color=lime] The Stone Fortresses of the South[/color]
Reach Level 30 to learn how unity and engineering build walls that never fall.

[color=yellow] The Sankofa Bird[/color]
Complete all quests to prove: \"It is not taboo to go back for what you have forgotten.\"

[center][color=yellow]═══════════════════════════════[/color][/center]

[center][i]Through mastering the art of organization, you will restore order from chaos.
Each level conquered brings back a piece of history.
Each achievement unlocked restores color to the continent.[/i][/center]"
fit_content = true
scroll_following = true

